#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:3
msgid "Run scripts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:5
msgid ""
"Run an app or a script in a temporary environment with ``pipx run``, without "
"installing it first. pipx downloads the package, caches the environment, and "
"runs the app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:10
msgid "Run a specific version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:12
msgid ""
"The ``PACKAGE`` argument is a `requirement specifier <https://packaging."
"python.org/en/latest/glossary/#term-Requirement-Specifier>`_, so you can pin "
"versions, ranges, or extras:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:16
msgid ""
"$ pipx run mpremote==1.20.0\n"
"$ pipx run --spec esptool==4.6.2 esptool.py\n"
"$ pipx run --spec 'esptool>=4.5' esptool.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:22
msgid "Quote any specifier that contains ``>``, ``<``, or spaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:26
msgid "Add extra dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:28
msgid ""
"``--with PKG`` adds packages to the temporary environment alongside the app. "
"Repeat it to add more:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:30
msgid "$ pipx run --with requests --with rich my-script.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:36
msgid "Pass arguments to Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:38
msgid ""
"``--python-args ARGS`` forwards arguments to the interpreter that runs the "
"app, rather than to the app itself:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:40
msgid "$ pipx run --python-args \"-X dev\" my-script.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:46
msgid "Run from source control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:48
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` accepts source-control URLs directly, with the same syntax as "
"``pipx install`` (see :ref:`install-from-source-control`). Using ``black`` "
"as an example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:51
msgid ""
"$ pipx run git+https://github.com/psf/black.git\n"
"$ pipx run git+https://github.com/psf/black.git@branch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:56
msgid ""
"Use ``--spec`` when the executable name differs from the package name or "
"when installing from an archive URL:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:58
msgid "$ pipx run --spec https://github.com/psf/black/archive/18.9b0.zip black"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:64
msgid "Run from a URL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:66
msgid "You can run ``.py`` files hosted anywhere:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:68
msgid ""
"$ pipx run https://gist.githubusercontent.com/cs01/"
"fa721a17a326e551ede048c5088f9e0f/"
"raw/6bdfbb6e9c1132b1c38fdd2f195d4a24c540c324/pipx-demo.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:76
msgid "Run a script with dependencies (PEP 723)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:78
msgid ""
"A script can declare its own dependencies with `inline script metadata "
"<https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/inline-script-"
"metadata/>`_. pipx reads the ``# /// script`` block and installs the listed "
"packages before running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:82
msgid ""
"# test.py\n"
"\n"
"# /// script\n"
"# dependencies = [\"requests\"]\n"
"# ///\n"
"\n"
"import sys\n"
"import requests\n"
"\n"
"project = sys.argv[1]\n"
"data = requests.get(f\"https://pypi.org/pypi/{project}/json\").json()\n"
"print(data[\"info\"][\"version\"])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:97
msgid ""
"$ pipx run test.py pipx\n"
"1.9.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:102
msgid ""
"pipx caches an environment keyed to the script's dependency list. Changing "
"the dependencies builds a fresh one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:106
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:108
msgid "$ pipx run pycowsay moo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/run-scripts.rst:112
msgid ""
"A successful run prints the app's own output; nothing is left installed "
"afterward."
msgstr ""
